To be fair, this is a pretty difficult situation to get out of.
Probably the correct answer (if there is any) would be to step back
towards the stairs.  If the monster hadn't fired before, then he
probably just saw you, so you were probably at the edge of his sight.
If you stepped back, then if he got the next move he'd have to chase
one step to get you back into sight.  (This assumes that he was coming
down a straight tunnel; if he had just come around a corner then you'd
likely still be in sight.)  You could also have moved perpendicular to
the direction from which the zap had come, since monsters, like you,
can only zap in the cardinal and diagonal directions.

Another possibility would have been to try healing.  Even if it
wouldn't be enough to get you all your hit points back, it might be
enough to cause you to survive the next turn, and the next zap might
have been enough to get you into the prayer HP-peril zone.

However, that would still leave the *next* turn, and wands of lightning
tend to have more than two zaps.  While I don't know what you were
carrying at the time, ultimately this is one of those emergency
situations where using unknown items in the hopes of getting something
which would allow you to survive.

Were you burdened or worse at the time?  If you were, then the proper
thing to have done would have been to not get burdened in the first
place.

Hm, looking through your story again, you were a level 8 Valk?  You
should have had a good number of hit points by this time, how much
damage did that first lightning shot do?

